.TH QUICK-HK 1 "September 2026" "YueKey 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
quick-hk \- configure and deploy Cantonese Quick input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quick-hk
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
YueKey supplies an offline Cantonese Quick Rime scheme for IBus and Fcitx5.
Commands modify the invoking user's profile, without restarting input daemons.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup, deploy
Stage and compile the scheme, then deploy with backups.
.TP
.B configure
Open the settings window. Use --set KEY=VALUE to edit from the command line,
--no-deploy with --set to save only, or --show to print preferences.
.TP
.B doctor
Check packages and profile status. Use --json for structured output.
.TP
.B uninstall
Restore unchanged managed files. Preserve user edits and learning databases.
.TP
.B reset-learning
Back up and remove YueKey learning. Stop the selected frontend first.
.TP
.B dictation setup
Download and verify SenseVoice Small Yue INT8, punctuation and VAD models;
prepare an isolated Python 3.12 CPU runtime using uv. Run as the desktop user.
.TP
.B dictation status [--json]
Show model readiness and the local dictation service state.
.TP
.B dictation serve
Run the session D-Bus controller. Normally started by desktop autostart or D-Bus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --frontend auto|ibus|fcitx5|both
Select profiles. Auto uses managed profiles, then the desktop environment.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Use an explicit preferences file.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/quick-hk/settings.toml
Preferences (honors XDG_CONFIG_HOME).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/quick-hk/
Backups and manifests (honors XDG_STATE_HOME).
.SH NOTES
Run as your desktop user. Activate Chinese (Rime) and choose the YueKey scheme
after setup. Desktop instructions are in /usr/share/doc/quick-hk-core/README.md.
